"answer": "According to the MedlinePlus summary \"Ureteral Disorders\" (MLP-5350), small amounts of urine normally flow from the ureters into the bladder about every 10 to 15 seconds. However, the document does not state what percentage of ureteral blockages require surgery rather than medicines; it only mentions that treatment may include medicines and, in severe cases, surgery."
